{"kind":"request","text":"DD-1: the descriptor digest follows the acts of a scope, and no\nrelease text.\n\nWhy. Ruling `c79545a3` makes a draft row with another descriptor\ndigest wait with no values, and `restore` stops there. So each\nchange of the digest costs a member every open form of that scope.\nThe fixture of C4 hashed the whole `dap.application.json`, and a\nversion-only release changed its value (`9616652e`). The real\ndescriptor has no builder yet, so the rule is free to set now.\n\nWhat. The step that builds the descriptor of section 10 of\n`notes/2026-11-14-act-environment.md` computes its digest from the\ncontent that section 10 lists, for the definition of one scope. The\ndigest covers no version text, no name, no path and no content of\nanother scope.\n\nBefore the build, a short proposal answers one question with\nnumbers from the three applications of the repository: one digest\nfor a scope, or one digest for each act. With one digest for a\nscope, a change of one act costs the open forms of every act of\nthat scope.","body":{"conditions":"A version-only release of an application keeps the digest of each scope, and one test pins it with a real release pair. A change of one act changes the digest as the proposal states. The proposal states the granularity (scope or act) with counts from Grow, Lending and Counter before any source. The digest reads definition bytes, never a path text. Starts with the step that builds the descriptor; it does not delay C4.","target_head":"6728059211cee75dc0f6fdd104ef52a44c5f7da0","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}